      "content": "The approach that emphasizes systemic injustices and power struggles is more effective for teaching kids history, as it prepares them for the complexities of the real world and encourages critical thinking about the ongoing struggles for equality and justice. By acknowledging the darker aspects of our nation's past, students can develop empathy and a nuanced understanding of the ongoing impact of historical events. This approach also helps to counterbalance the simplistic, feel-good narratives that can be misleading and disempowering.",
